\title{shadshiny: 'shadcn/ui' Components for 'Shiny'}
\description{
A complete port of the shadcn/ui design system for Shiny: 72 accessible,
themeable components implemented in framework-free CSS and vanilla
JavaScript, wrapped as native R functions with Shiny input bindings. It
coexists with Bootstrap 5 and bslib, including automatic dark-mode
synchronization.
}
\section{Getting started}{

Wrap your UI in \code{\link[=page_shad]{page_shad()}} to attach the asset bundle and theme scope,
then use the \verb{shad_*()} component constructors. Read bound values as
\verb{input$<inputId>} and update them from the server with the \verb{update_shad_*()}
helpers.
}

\section{Load order & the uniform contract}{

All assets ship as a single bundled \link[htmltools:htmlDependency]{htmlDependency}
(\code{\link[=shadshiny_deps]{shadshiny_deps()}}) whose files load in a fixed order: tokens, base and
animation CSS, then component CSS/JS, with the Shiny binding layer last. Every
stateful component root carries \code{data-shad="<name>"}; its JS instance exposes
\code{getValue()}/\code{setValue()} (plus \code{open()}/\code{close()} for overlays) and
dispatches a bubbling \code{shad:change} event that the generic Shiny input binding
subscribes to.
}

\section{Theming}{

Colours come from \verb{--shad-*} OKLCH custom properties. Switch palette with
\code{\link[=shad_theme_preset]{shad_theme_preset()}} or the \code{theme_preset} argument of \code{\link[=page_shad]{page_shad()}}, and at
runtime with \code{\link[=update_shad_theme]{update_shad_theme()}}. Dark mode keys off both \code{.dark} and
\verb{[data-bs-theme="dark"]}, so \code{bslib::input_dark_mode()} works with no glue.
}

